{"seq":18,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-no-work-habits-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:57:49.441Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"628367c1cb52d08483bc7508ddb24820aba37291b21f74cb8c76e37de05893ef","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I can see (the North and Central team digests in the shared files). I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments from the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through fine. There was also a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other QFL notes (the 9/14/2025 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) have no ticket numbers. Some things I left out on purpose:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoff digest are Marrow tickets, not QFL.\n• Marcus's 2025-08-11 intel note is about Quarendon Freightways, a different company that isn't a customer. It isn't Moss's note anyway.\n\nMoss has no personal notes folder I can see, and Moss hasn't posted anything in the channels you're in. So these two are everything I could find."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
